WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.110
After arriving in Hong Kong,
Amuro ran into Mirai...

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:40.310
...who was waiting with her children
for a ride to outer space.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.820
About that time, a giant mobile suit,
the Psyco Gundam...

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.830
...left the Sudori to invade Hong Kong.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.660
Kamille was left with a feeling of
aversion for this enemy.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:58.120
Mirai Captured

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.550
<i>Four, get back here!</i>

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.150
<i>If you don't stop acting selfishly,</i>
<i>you won't get your memory back.</i>

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.050
You're the Psyco's pilot!

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.290
I've got to bring her back.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.640
Have you loaded all mobile suit fixtures?

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.680
All that's left is the loading of the Dodais.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.640
I'm very impressed with Luio & Co.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.180
Impressive indeed.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.180
I don't see Kamille and Amuro.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.410
Oh, they have things to take care of.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:55.960
There, Cheimin!

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.130
Wow!

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.570
Is it your idea to have me
board the Audhumla?

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.040
That's right.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.580
But I'm sure Hayato feels the same way.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.630
You haven't got your flight ticket yet,
have you?

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.580
I'm very grateful for your consideration.
However...!

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.680
The worse the war situation...

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.720
...the more difficult it will become
to get to space.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:20.480
Who knows when you'd be able to see
Bright again?

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.420
Sure, I want to see my husband.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:26.890
But I can't take the children into
battle zones just to see him.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.060
There!

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.400
Oh no!

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.760
Let me think about it a little more, Amuro.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:38.770
Mirai.

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:39.500
Mommy!

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.730
The glider flew away.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:42.870
Oh, my.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.570
Amuro, we should get going.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:48.620
The Audhumla will be departing
by tomorrow morning. So...!

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.180
Thank you, Amuro.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.290
- This way!
- What's keeping you?!

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.220
No way!

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.800
Four Marine Hizacks
have been dispatched.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.140
Good.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.910
Does this satisfy you, Miss Cornell?

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.770
I'm very grateful to have you allocate
that many of your staff for us.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.250
You realize, enormous funds
have been invested in Four.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:30.890
It pains me to have to hire you special
service officers to look for a lost child...

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.890
...but we're pressed to the brink here.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.020
No, this is a great chance for us.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.560
If we can take advantage of Four's actions
to take over the Audhumla...

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.190
...without damaging it, Hong Kong
will escape being burnt down.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:46.370
As the Hong Kong operatives we must also
show some results to the Titans.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.380
If Four is a complete Cyber-Newtype...

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.380
...she will surely make contact
with the enemy.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.680
Dr. Murasame is a very
capable person.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:14.090
She seems to be having fun.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:16.470
Amuro!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.440
- Goodbye!
- Goodbye!

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.870
Those people are neither A.E.U.G.
nor military.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.240
Why are you trying to get them
aboard the Audhumla, Amuro?

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.510
You probably wouldn't understand, but...!

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.350
<i>Audhumla? Amuro?</i>

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.880
That's Hathaway's airplane!

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.010
That!

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.880
Don't lose it again.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.420
Thank you, ma'am.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:38.820
You're very kind. Thank you very much.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:39.760
No problem.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:43.390
That's great! You got the glider back.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.370
<i>Who is this woman?</i>

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.100
<i>Is he Amuro Ray?</i>

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.000
Aren't you returning?

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.430
What are you doing in a place like this?!

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.240
I'm here on orders from Director Hayato.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.830
Mr. Amuro, why won't you tell her
to be quiet?

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:58.940
<i>So he is Amuro.</i>

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:01.880
<i>Then could he be the one</i>
<i>who was piloting the Gundam Mk. II?</i>

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:06.420
Everyone is worried when Amuro
goes out without telling anyone.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.390
Especially if he's with you.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.650
I came to keep Amuro in check.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:13.090
All right, then please return immediately!

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.320
Sure, we'll return.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:19.130
<i>Is he the one who made me uncomfortable?</i>

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.040
Hey, you!

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.410
Mind driving me to the old city?

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:32.050
Sure, I can take you.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.610
That would be great.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.460
Do you know that couple?

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:48.550
I don't know that man and woman
who lick each other's wounds!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.630
Oh, I get it.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.220
Yes, I'm sure you do.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:57.330
How pathetic.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:06:59.310
That's exactly how I feel.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.980
Four is on the move.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:07.850
Amuro Ray is personally acquainted with
a woman with two children...

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.880
...staying at the Coral Oriental vessel.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:13.890
Do you like gliders?

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.580
I like anything that flies.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.820
So do I.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.980
My name's Kamille.
Nice to meet you.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:20.820
I'm Four Murasame.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:23.860
Four Murasame? That's a difficult name.

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:26.090
I can't help it.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.070
That's the name I was given.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.570
You're right about that.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:31.400
Kamille...!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.530
What a kind name.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.500
You don't like your own name, do you?

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:39.640
Why do you say that?

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.150
It's written all over your face.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:42.810
Really?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:53.050
<i>What would be the best</i>
<i>thing for us to do, Bright?</i>

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.320
<i>Would it be better</i>
<i>if we didn't go to space?</i>

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.800
Mommy?

00:07:58.430 --> 00:07:59.660
I brought my dirty clothes.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:00.830
What about Cheimin's clothes?

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:02.370
Here!

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.400
You're such a good girl, Cheimin.
Let's go.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.680
Who are you people?!

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.050
Stop it, what are you doing?!

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.680
Don't you dare touch the children!

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:25.760
Roger!!

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:27.490
Did you track down Four?

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.790
Can you get our wireless connected
with the broadcast station?

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.630
That can easily be done.

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.130
What's happening with Four?!

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.690
This is our chance to stop
the A.E.U.G. cold.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:38.830
Once we commence our plans,
Four will show up.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:44.000
Aren't you getting off yet?

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.640
You'll buy me something to drink,
won't you?

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:46.700
Huh?!

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:47.840
There's a shop.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.520
You want to know the truth?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.580
I'll go wherever you go.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:55.680
Even if you're going to join
that person I saw earlier.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:57.390
Four...

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.350
Are you a fan of Amuro?

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.950
What if I were?

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.160
I'd be jealous!

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.170
Did you believe me?

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:11.570
Naturally.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:12.610
Sorry.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.980
The truth is I was looking for someone.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:15.940
Who?

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.170
Someone who understands me.

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:23.980
<i>This message is directed to the A.E.U.G.</i>
<i>and all of their sympathizers.</i>

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:27.180
<i>I am the acting captain of the Sudori,</i>
<i>Captain Ben Wooder.</i>

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:28.880
What's this?

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.550
<i>Unless you people hand over the Audhumla</i>
<i>to us within 24 hours...</i>

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.600
<i>...we will indiscriminately open fire</i>
<i>on the city of New Hong Kong!</i>

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.630
Amuro!

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.870
<i>If you should unfairly decide</i>
<i>to attack us...</i>

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.880
<i>...we will no longer be able</i>
<i>to guarantee the lives of the hostages.</i>

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:53.910
What?!

00:09:55.620 --> 00:10:00.150
<i>The hostages are former</i>
<i>White Base Captain Bright Noa's wife...</i>

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.550
<i>...Mirai Yashima and their two children.</i>

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:07.890
Amuro!

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.520
- Don't throw stuff out the window!
- Keep your hands off the children!

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.130
I want you to contact the Audhumla!

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:13.830
What are you going to do?!

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:16.700
Are you a member of the A.E.U.G.?

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:17.740
By chance.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.700
Do you pilot mobile suits?

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:20.640
More or less.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:25.440
I'm getting off.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.370
Yeah, it's not safe.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.280
- Take care.
- Thank you.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.050
We'll meet again, won't we?

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.680
I'd like that.

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.060
Sorry!!

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:42.620
Tell Ben Wooder that
I can't stand these tactics!

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.930
If you don't like it,
then take part in it yourself.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.970
This kind of operation is
none of my business!

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.670
You'll be executed for fleeing
from the enemy!

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.560
I'm presently checking out the enemy!

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:53.400
So you don't like to cooperate with us?

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.540
Hey!

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:58.840
You saw me keep an Audhumla pilot here
with your own eyes!

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:01.610
- That guy was a pilot?
- Of course!

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:04.650
<i>If we went in the Audhumla</i>
<i>to negotiate with the enemy...</i>

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.690
<i>...we'd be practically handing over</i>
<i>this Garuda transport!</i>

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.090
But they have hostages!

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:10.820
<i>What's a mere three or four hostages?!</i>

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.550
We have an incoming phone call.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.690
Just a moment!

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:15.920
Hayato here!

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.260
<i>It's Beltorchika!</i>

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.630
This is absurd for you to be calling
by telephone!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.460
Hang up at once!

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:23.600
Amuro's... Amuro's gone
to the enemy's hovercraft!

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.470
I tried to stop him, but he wouldn't listen.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:27.100
He went alone!

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.400
Okay, Beltorchika!

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.410
You're to return to the Stockpile Base!

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:32.500
Got that?!

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.450
<i>Why's everyone so swayed by sympathy?!</i>

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.780
<i>Please do not forget the causes</i>
<i>of the A.E.U.G.!</i>

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:39.220
We haven't forgotten!

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.650
<i>I'm going there!</i>

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:43.050
- We're moving the Audhumla!
- Yes, sir!

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:47.790
I don't know how important
these hostages are to them...

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:50.830
...but we can't leave Hong Kong
in a sea of fire as a result.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:57.530
Please don't get Luio & Co.'s
Stockpile Base mixed up in this.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.200
We won't!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.580
I want to see the person in charge!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.250
I'm in charge.

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.290
You say you want to exchange hostages.
Can you elaborate?!

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:20.460
I'm Captain Amuro Ray.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.160
I should be of great value to you
as a hostage.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.090
Is he telling the truth?

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.760
I recognize the face.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:28.700
I'm sure you'd rather not be known
for using unfair tactics...

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.700
...like taking women and children
for hostages!

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:33.410
Very well! Bring out the mother
and children.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:34.440
Yes sir!

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.710
Is it true that Amuro is here?

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.650
You heard his voice, didn't you?

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.140
<i>Which vessel?</i>

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:53.250
It's from the Mayor of Hong Kong.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:54.300
This is the Audhumla.

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:55.850
Stephanie Luio speaking.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:58.230
Make sure all mobile suits are ready to
counterattack anytime!

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:00.290
Upon the honor of Luio & Co....

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.300
...we will have the Audhumla
flee Hong Kong!

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:05.430
This way, the city will avoid
getting involved in this war.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:06.710
Amuro!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:08.370
Mirai.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:09.380
Amuro.

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:11.340
The Audhumla has many qualified pilots
on board.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:12.440
- Go.
- Okay.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:16.350
It's an honor to be joined by a former hero.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:18.540
Why must you go to this extent
to seize the Audhumla?

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:20.920
I don't know about politics...

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:24.650
...but as a soldier, it's only natural
for me to follow my orders, right?

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:27.560
But the present government
is trying to destroy Earth!

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:31.860
Mirai! Hurry to shore!

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.760
Right! I'm going!

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.870
What's wrong?

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.540
Amuro!

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:53.550
Director Hayato!

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:57.260
<i>The proposal presented by Hong Kong City</i>
<i>is an insult to us.</i>

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:00.620
<i>Should the Audhumla try to leave</i>
<i>Hong Kong at this stage...</i>

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.630
<i>...we plan to have</i>
<i>the four hostages slaughtered!</i>

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.790
There are more hostages?

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:07.070
<i>We'll first take the life</i>
<i>of Bright Noa's wife!</i>

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:11.460
<i>I took part in this operation because</i>
<i>I was told that I could fight as a pilot.</i>

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:16.370
<i>More than anything, Murasame Laboratory</i>
<i>has something very important to me.</i>

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:21.640
<i>In order to get that back, I can't have</i>
<i>some snob like Ben Wooder get in my way.</i>

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.280
What's that?

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.650
Kamille?

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.660
Send out a Dodai!
We're bringing Kamille in!

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.200
Kamille, I'm glad you made it back!

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:50.180
How did they end up with
an additional hostage?!

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:55.180
Amuro went to trade places with Mirai,
but they ended up capturing them all.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:57.650
Mr. Amuro's way too optimistic!

00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:59.480
Don't be so hard on him, Kamille!

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:02.390
If we play our cards wrong,
the hostages will be dead!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.860
The Sudori may already have a trap set up.

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:08.490
Isn't there the chance we may be facing
an enemy other than the Sudori?

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:11.730
Both Mirai and Amuro
are very important people to us.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.100
I know. I'll need a flawless strategy.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:15.070
Kamille!

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.690
This international city of Hong Kong...!

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:18.530
I've figured out a way.

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:21.540
A plan that uses the Mk. II to save
the hostages and Hong Kong as well.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.170
I-Is it possible?

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:25.340
We'll hand over the Audhumla.

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:26.400
That's crazy!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:29.280
If we surrender now, our efforts
to this point will have been wasted!

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:33.010
We can't win by force, so we'll
pretend to be surrendering.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.280
Director.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:36.790
Let's do it.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:38.220
Can you remain calm?

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.190
If you can't, I cannot authorize this.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.420
You have no authority in this,
Miss Stephanie.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:43.360
Kamille!

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.190
I'm joking.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:48.290
I'll try. I'll calmly observe
the situation before I fight.

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:49.630
You're sure?

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:50.830
Of course.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.410
<i>What is this kindness I feel?</i>

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.600
<i>She has the scent of a woman,</i>
<i>different from that of Four.</i>

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.370
<i>I feel strength in her.</i>

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.810
We're going to save everyone!

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:00.310
I'm counting on you!

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:04.280
- Stephanie, thank you for your kind words.
- Nonsense.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.250
I was only telling the truth.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:11.460
Director Hayato!

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.260
I need to know the exact
timing for my take-off.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:14.290
<i>Roger!</i>

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:24.300
I doubt a mobility test has been done
underwater.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.430
<i>Be cautious of the water pressure,</i>
<i>Kamille!</i>

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:27.370
Roger!

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.000
Kamille. Let's do it!

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:39.550
Enemies are also underwater.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.390
Here they come.

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.070
Very compliant.

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:54.260
Looks like you won't have to die
after all, Captain!

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:56.300
Did the Audhumla come?

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:05.410
Are they coming?

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:13.280
It's as Miss Stephanie was saying.
Could there be other enemies, too?

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.790
My head.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:29.130
Must I always rely on that Cornell
to get rid of this headache?

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:34.500
Will Director Hayato back me up?

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:35.770
Mommy!

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.170
It'll be all right.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:41.870
Look, the men from that big airplane
will come and get us.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.780
Will they also save Mr. Amuro?

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:44.650
Of course.

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:51.020
<i>Hayato. What's he thinking?</i>

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.330
This should make it clear
that we have no intentions of fighting.

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:59.530
There are enemies hiding underwater,
aren't there?

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:00.730
Probably.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:05.260
- But Kamille...!
- I'm sure he'll take care of things.

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.340
Looks like they're surrendering.

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:13.110
Hmm... Call the Sudori over
and get started with our takeover.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.220
Damn!

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:30.630
Mommy!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:31.600
Hathaway!

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.500
- Help!
- Hathaway!

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:40.010
That's one!

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:48.710
Don't let that hostage get away!
Get him!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.280
That's Mr. Amuro!

00:18:59.390 --> 00:19:00.620
Where's Mrs. Mirai?

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:13.570
Those mobile suits are
for underwater use!

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.600
Hathaway!

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:26.640
He sank!

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.020
You're free now!

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:41.800
Amuro! Over here! Amuro!

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:44.900
There!

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:50.970
- Give him mouth-to-mouth!
- A-Amuro.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:53.940
Ready to send out mobile suits!

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:55.910
- Audhumla, prepare to leave waters!
- Yes, sir!

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:10.160
What are you doing, Namicar?!

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:13.670
Now that we've lost our hostages,
our plan has officially failed!

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:17.430
Aren't you feeling seasick?

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:18.770
Huh? No.

00:20:22.210 --> 00:20:24.070
I've got to drag these guys out of the sea!

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.380
That's three!

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:05.520
Whenever there is a calm period,
this always follows.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:20.400
Amuro!

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:21.430
Beltorchika!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.790
I'm so glad you're okay.

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:26.500
- A Gundam!
- Can he land it?

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:34.450
Wow!

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:36.770
Impressive, Kamille.

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:38.250
Is he like you, Amuro?

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:40.750
No, nothing like me.

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.050
But he's got much more promise
than myself.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:48.690
Were you driving it?

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:50.230
That's right. Are you all right?

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:52.700
Mhm! Hathaway's feeling better, too!

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:55.560
Is that so! I'm happy to hear that.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:57.130
It's all your fault!

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:00.370
Ever since you came, Amuro's forgotten
about the A.E.U.G....

00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:02.600
...and even gets himself into
this sort of danger!

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:05.200
That's not true, Amuro isn't such
a weak person.

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:07.410
Beltorchika, forget it.

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:11.150
I can't understand!

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:12.550
Hayato!

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:14.050
I'm glad to see you're all right, Mirai!

00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:16.510
Thank you, Hayato!

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:18.520
We're okay, thanks to Amuro and Kamille.

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.120
Kamille! You really shone out there!

00:22:23.430 --> 00:22:24.800
Thank you very much.

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:27.530
Great work, Captain Amuro.

00:22:27.940 --> 00:22:30.430
Thank you. Same goes for you.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.510 --> 00:23:49.100
Kamille and Four are unable to obtain
new memories...

00:23:49.180 --> 00:23:52.310
...from the short time they are allowed
to spend together.

00:23:52.920 --> 00:23:55.380
The bittersweet impurities of their
youthful days...

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:57.420
...fade away in the flames of Hong Kong.

00:23:57.750 --> 00:24:00.250
The two only discover that
their inescapable fate...

00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:02.260
...is to become enemies.

00:24:02.690 --> 00:24:07.500
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Cinderella Four".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Cinderella Four

00:24:07.830 --> 00:24:12.390
You will see the tears of time.
